examples.question_text:
Red and blue paint are mixed in the ratio $5:3$. How much red paint is needed with $11.4$ L of blue paint?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\node[left] at (-0.15,1.2) {Red};
\foreach \x in {0,0.8,1.6,2.4,3.2} {\draw (\x,0.9) rectangle ++(0.8,0.6);}
\node[right] at (4.15,1.2) {$?$};
\node[left] at (-0.15,0.3) {Blue};
\foreach \x in {0,0.8,1.6} {\draw (\x,0) rectangle ++(0.8,0.6);}
\node[right] at (2.55,0.3) {$11.4$ L};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Blue paint represents $3$ parts.
$3\text{ parts}=11.4\text{ L}$
$1\text{ part}=11.4\div3=3.8\text{ L}$
$5\text{ parts}=5\times3.8=19\text{ L}$
Use $19$ L of red paint.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\node[left] at (-0.15,1.2) {Red};
\foreach \x in {0,0.8,1.6,2.4,3.2} {\draw (\x,0.9) rectangle ++(0.8,0.6);}
\foreach \x in {0.4,1.2,2,2.8,3.6} {\node at (\x,1.2) {$3.8$};}
\node[right] at (4.15,1.2) {$19$ L};
\node[left] at (-0.15,0.3) {Blue};
\foreach \x in {0,0.8,1.6} {\draw (\x,0) rectangle ++(0.8,0.6);}
\foreach \x in {0.4,1.2,2} {\node at (\x,0.3) {$3.8$};}
\node[right] at (2.55,0.3) {$11.4$ L};
\node[below] at (2,-0.35) {Each cell represents $3.8$ L.};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A rectangle has width:length $=5:7$ and length $26.6$ cm. Find its perimeter.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.2,3);
\node[below] at (2.1,0) {$26.6$ cm};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$?$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Length represents $7$ parts.
$1\text{ part}=26.6\div7=3.8\text{ cm}$
Width: $5\times3.8=19\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.2,3);
\node[below] at (2.1,0) {$26.6$ cm};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$19$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P=2\times(19+26.6)\\&=91.2\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

examples.question_text:
Three landmarks $A$, $B$ and $C$ lie on a straight road, in that order. The ratio $AB:BC$ is $3:4$, and $AB=24$ km. Find $AC$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \x/\label in {0/A,3/B,7/C} {\fill[black] (\x,0) circle (2pt);\node[below] at (\x,-0.1) {$\label$};}
\draw[<->] (0,0.6)--(3,0.6);
\node[above] at (1.5,0.6) {$24$ km};
\draw[<->] (0,1.4)--(7,1.4);
\node[above] at (3.5,1.4) {$?$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
$AB$ represents $3$ parts.
$3\text{ parts}=24\text{ km}$
$1\text{ part}=24\div3=8\text{ km}$
$AC$ represents $3+4=7$ parts.
$7\text{ parts}=7\times8=56\text{ km}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \x/\label in {0/A,3/B,7/C} {\fill[black] (\x,0) circle (2pt);\node[below] at (\x,-0.1) {$\label$};}
\draw[<->] (0,0.6)--(3,0.6);
\node[above] at (1.5,0.6) {$24$ km};
\draw[<->] (3,0.6)--(7,0.6);
\node[above] at (5,0.6) {$32$ km};
\draw[<->] (0,1.4)--(7,1.4);
\node[above] at (3.5,1.4) {$56$ km};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
